      "problem": "Select the correct options in the truth table below and use this to determine whether $(P∧Q)∧(¬P∨Q)$ is a contradiction.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,P∧Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨Q\\,$ | $\\,(P∧Q)∧(¬P∨Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-4}} |\n\nAccording to the table, $(P∧Q)∧(¬P∨Q)$ \n{{field-5}}\nalways false. Therefore, it \n{{field-6}} \na contradiction.",
